A fly in the ointment
So, in some ways, the quarter was pretty solid for the world's largest pure-play public uranium miner. But you have to take the results with a grain of salt, too. For example, despite the company's long-term contracts, management pointed out that uranium prices are near decade lows. Although Cameco is insulated from that for now, it doesn't bode well for the future unless something in the market changes{g}.{r}
