Shortstop Troy Tulowitzki turned in a clutch play in the ninth, throwing out Skip Schumaker — although replays clearly showed that Schumaker was safe as he slid into first base. However, it was his two errors that were eating at Tulo after the game. ��I just had a bad day defensively, no way around it,�� he said. It was just the second time in Tulowitzki��s career that he made two errors in a game. The first was Aug. 6, 2007, against Milwaukee.
Triple time.
Catcher Yorvit Torrealba tripled off the base of the right-field wall to lead off the sixth. It was his first three-bagger since Aug. 28, 2007, at San Francisco.
El Hombre.
Cardinals slugger Albert Pujols continues to show why he has inherited Stan Musial��s crown as ��the man�� in St. Louis. Pujols hit a three-run double in the third, making him 10-for-16 (.625) with 34 RBIs with the bases full this season.
